Release idle TPROXY UDP local sockets and stop their reader goroutines.
Based on upstream PR #3344:
https://github.com/MetaCubeX/mihomo/pull/3344

Downstream hardening: atomically retire only the expected socket, invalidate
closed cached sockets before one write retry, and publish before reading.
Creation uses a held per-key mutex instead of a lossy condition notification;
NAT-entry and creation-lock replacements are checked before publishing/cleanup.
No socket I/O runs inside a map Compute callback.

